Here is a basic template for a denial script that redirects users to a custom error page. You'll need to replace `[URL]` with the path to your actual site or service.

```perl
# A simple deny-by-default script
use LWP::Simple;

my $response = LWP::Simple->new->get('https://example.com');
if ($response->is_success) {
    # Continue normal flow
} else {
    # Redirect to error page
    $response->redirect(
        'https://example.com/error.html'
    );
}
```

If you want to customize the message, write the error HTML in `/error.html` and set the header in the script above.
